08591e4983bf22e802c1b10a4","event_uuid":"6f99ef6d-c3b0-4c1b-b2dc-1566cc85fbf6","position":{"commit_sha":"d4f773f362a881d72a8b2d9336a0176423439200","position":"1788946028331231740-6f99ef6d-c3b0-4c1b-b2dc-1566cc85fbf6"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIGNNmnI/WYNJAOKH9yvo0l+tMYJR2tK2UV4H8ReXBQU5 rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com rotated-20260907"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Additional advisory from c6ce plan-review re-attestation (non-blocking): the corroborator hand-rolls process-group termination (_terminate: killpg SIGTERM -> 1s grace -> killpg SIGKILL -> wait) instead of delegating to rebar._proc.reap_process_group, the harness's named single source of truth for reaping a timed-out grounding child + its group (bug d843). Consider delegating to reap_process_group when addressing the subprocess-memory-bound item, since both touch _run's subprocess lifecycle.","timestamp":1788604262161557001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Additional minor cleanup surfaced while certifying the REB-640 epic: leaf 08ab's description still contains an AC verify-command referencing the pre-rename ADR path 'test -f docs/adr/0111-terraform-structural-grounding.md' (the terraform ADR actually landed at 0115). 08ab's file_impact was corrected to 0115, but the AC verify-command prose in its description was left as-is (advisory only; the completion gate does not execute it, and 08ab's original close passed with the file already at 0115). Cosmetic doc-consistency fix for a future pass.","timestamp":1788608048841919001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Operator ruling 2026-09-08: Option 1 approved — one combined cleanup change addressing all three PS2 advisories together: (1) bound corroborator subprocess memory via incremental pipe reads, reusing rebar._proc.reap_process_group per bug d843; (2) remove the dead env filter; (3) add the match-path non-disclosure test. Respect ADR 0115 (this is the single sanctioned subprocess; bounded/redacted execution).","timestamp":1788909120179522001}],"created_at":1788602441866463001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"e5e22f16-beea-4d97-9778-d201a99eb2ee","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"c6ce-4d8d-1c12-47cc"},{"link_uuid":"6f99ef6d-c3b0-4c1b-b2dc-1566cc85fbf6","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"b897-0c36-46d8-44ad"}],"description":"## Context\nFollow-up advisories from Gerrit change 2672 patchset 2 identified three cleanup items for the Terraform structural grounding corroborator. Operator ruling 2026-09-08 approved one combined change:\n\n1. Bound peak memory for the sanctioned `terraform-config-inspect` subprocess. The current `terraform_corroborator._run` uses `proc.communicate(timeout=...)`, so stdout/stderr are buffered before the post-hoc size cap can run. Replace that with incremental pipe reads under the existing deadline, aborting to the existing worker-failure/abstain path when either stream exceeds its cap. Use non-blocking `selectors.DefaultSelector` registration for stdout and stderr so both pipes are drained without deadlock, and keep byte counters before appending chunks to the retained buffers.\n2. Reuse `rebar._proc.reap_process_group` for timeout and output-cap abort cleanup per bug d843. The local `_terminate` helper should disappear; the subprocess remains ADR 0115's single sanctioned Terraform corroborator subprocess.\n3. Remove the dead `_minimal_env` conjunct `and not _drop_env(k)`: `_KEEP_ENV` is a closed allowlist and none of its members match any `_DROP_ENV_PREFIXES` entry through `_drop_env`.\n4. Strengthen match-path non-disclosure coverage so a positive declaration match never leaks the fixture value `SECRET` in evidence or receipt output.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [x] `src/rebar/grounding/terraform_corroborator.py` drains stdout and stderr incrementally with `selectors.DefaultSelector` or an equivalent dual-pipe nonblocking mechanism, enforces `MAX_STDOUT`/`MAX_STDERR` before unbounded buffering, and returns the existing abstain/worker-failure result when a cap is exceeded.\n- [x] Timeout and cap cleanup delegates process-group reaping to `rebar._proc.reap_process_group`; no local hand-rolled killpg loop remains.\n- [x] `_minimal_env` keeps only the intended allowlisted environment variables without the misleading dead `_drop_env` conjunct.\n- [x] RED coverage in `tests/unit/grounding/test_terraform_corroborator.py` fails on current main for over-cap stdout and over-cap stderr producers before the implementation, then passes after the incremental reader is added.\n- [x] RED coverage in `tests/unit/grounding/test_terraform_corroborator.py` fails if the exact-match path leaks `SECRET` into evidence or receipt output, then passes with the existing redaction contract preserved.\n- [x] Targeted verification passes: `checked: env -u GIT_CONFIG_COUNT -u GIT_CONFIG_KEY_0 -u GIT_CONFIG_VALUE_0 PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" python -m pytest -q tests/unit/grounding/test_terraform_corroborator.py`.\n- [x] Final gate passes before push: `checked: env -u GIT_CONFIG_COUNT -u GIT_CONFIG_KEY_0 -u GIT_CONFIG_VALUE_0 PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" make verify PYTEST_WORKERS=2`.\n","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/grounding/terraform_corroborator.py","reason":"Bound the sanctioned Terraform corroborator subprocess output memory, use shared process-group reaping, and remove the dead env-filter conjunct."},{"path":"tests/unit/grounding/test_terraform_corroborator.py","reason":"Add regression coverage for output cap handling and match-path non-disclosure."}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["parent","a374-849c-c8f2-4234"],["relates_to","b897-0c36-46d8-44ad"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"","parent_status_uuid":"11df5949-e0cc-4ad2-b99c-bea7d1707997","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":[],"ticket_id":"ca1f-88ee-6211-4bff","ticket_type":"task","title":"Corroborator PS2 advisories: bound subprocess memory, dead env filter, match-path non-disclosure test","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["185d910f-34e1-437b-830e-ec9134be0b96","5315975f-eff3-45e9-8407-2f4ab178023c","994a54df-d236-4355-8d15-89dcfe08a5a5","cf5734f0-2a08-425f-8d6a-559089171e15","42ecc306-5542-48b0-b756-e72f52c21f6e","bbe3bfb9-33b2-42aa-9a5d-2253a14f1ee9","531fd2ba-5125-4fc9-9d4c-2ee63fab3e26","11df5949-e0cc-4ad2-b99c-bea7d1707997","a8b7c564-e407-48bb-8d96-bf5cbdd74de1","61acb116-48ce-4fd1-bded-544669108b3f","6f99ef6d-c3b0-4c1b-b2dc-1566cc85fbf6"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1788946028331231741,"uuid":"4416fca2-b332-4a99-beb1-4e1a07e42cb9"}